{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfbpsnQrtS9nyYJ7yLoPz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe consolidation itself is well-executed and idiomatic: one `OwnerIdentity` helper, one `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` step, one exception, one handler, one escalation YAML — mirroring the single-responsibility step pattern the codebase already uses, with the check correctly repositioned after `AssignHousehold` and clearly documented. Two structural issues keep it from clean, though:\n\n**1. `OwnerIdentity.keyOf(String, String, String)` is public but has no caller (speculative API surface).**\nThe only production consumers are `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` and `OwnerMapper`, and both call `of(Owner)`. `keyOf` is invoked only internally by `of`. Exposing a second public entry point with no external use adds API surface a maintainer has to reason about and keep in sync (\"which one do I call, and why are there two?\"). Unless something outside this diff (e.g. a test) genuinely needs the raw-component form, make `keyOf` private and let `of` be the single public \"source of truth\" the class's own Javadoc advertises. If a test does use it, that's worth a one-line note on the method so the public-ness is explained rather than looking accidental.\n\n**2. `OwnerIdentity` lives in `rest.function.owner` but is now consumed across layers.**\nWith the mapper mapping added, `OwnerMapper` (mapper layer) now reaches into `rest.function.owner` — the request-handling layer — to compute a DTO field. The other mapper expressions reference model-level derivations (`MembershipLevel.of`, `Regions.localityOf`, `ContactPreference.of`). `identityKey` has become a genuinely cross-cutting derived attribute of an owner (used by both the responder/mapper and the pipeline check), so its home in the function package is now a slight layering inversion. Consider whether it belongs alongside those model-level derivation helpers instead, so the mapper doesn't depend on a pipeline-function class. This is lower-severity than (1) — the existing `OwnerTelephone`/`OwnerHousehold` helpers already sit in that package — but the new mapper dependency is what tips it over.\n\nNeither is a correctness issue; fixing (1) at minimum would make the new class read as intended."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20313,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20313},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d280b2e7-1815-455a-95d7-6920f76040e9","uuid":"16f5799b-4b21-46bb-953d-7c5b5897781a","timestamp":"2026-10-01T16:24:06.420Z","request_id":"req_011CfbpsmyKp1o48DSK5J5mk"}
